# Clean-room reverse engineering

The tracker reproduces Jira *behavior*, never Jira *code or assets*.

## Allowed sources
- Public Jira Cloud REST API v3 documentation, fetched through context7
  (`/websites/developer_atlassian_cloud_jira_platform_rest_v3`).
- Observations of request/response shapes from an instance you are licensed to use,
  captured by REA `inspect-web-page` with `--include-json-body-shapes` (shapes only).
- Our own black-box tests against `tracker/`.

## Forbidden
- Decompiling, deobfuscating, or exporting Atlassian scripts (`export-web-scripts`,
  `recover-javascript-sources`) and pasting any of that code, CSS, icons, or copy here.
- Storing captured tokens, cookies, storage values, or customer data. REA warns that
  accessibility text, console text, and script content can contain secrets.
- Using a target the operator is not authorized to analyze.

## Process
1. Write the observed behavior into `tracker/spec/jira-rest-v3.md` with its source.
2. Implement from the spec only. A second agent session should do the implementation
   when the first one looked at captures.
3. Mark anything inferred rather than documented as `내부 정의` in the spec.

```text
❌ "Copied the board drag handler from the captured bundle."
✅ "Spec §Transitions: POST /transitions returns 204; board calls it on drop."
```
